## Under the types (root TypedApp): `U8.to(0 + 0, 3)`'s first argument is a
## U8 by the checker (the literals the call makes one), and `Iter.fold`'s an
## Iter, so all three calls are proven; but `(0 + 0).to(3).fold(...)` leaves
## the sum's type to default, and the one confirm fails. (A bare literal is
## no candidate; a sum of them is, and only the compiler or an expect sees
## it.) The file goes back to rounds: the line's two calls stay, with the
## compiler's reason, and the other is still turned.
ProvenFails := [].{
	bytes : List(U8)
	bytes = Iter.fold(U8.to(0 + 0, 3), [], |acc, b| acc.append(b))

	size : List(U8) -> U64
	size = |b| b.len()
}

expect ProvenFails.size(ProvenFails.bytes) == 4
